-- title:
--   Signed coordinate symmetries of the cubic lattice
-- statement:
--   Symmetries of $\mathbb Z^3$ generated by permuting coordinates, flipping signs and translating, together with their action on bonds.
--
--   1. **Internal bonds.** For a finite set $D$ of vertices, the internal bonds are the bonds $(x,i)$ with $x$ and $x+e_i$ both in $D$.
--   2. **Signed symmetries.** A signed symmetry is a permutation $\pi$ of $\{0,1,2\}$, signs $s_i$ and a shift $c$, acting on vertices by
--   $$
--   x\mapsto\bigl(c_i+s_i\,x_{\pi(i)}\bigr)_i ,
--   $$
--   which is a bijection of $\mathbb Z^3$.
--   3. **Bonds.** The induced bijection on bonds maps a bond to the bond joining the images of its endpoints, re-indexed from its lower endpoint (an extra shift corrects reversed directions). A bond $e$ has endpoints $\{x,y\}$ if $\{x,y\}=\{e_1,e_1+e_{e_2}\}$.
